{
  "sn4.6:0.1": "Linked Discourses 4.6 ",
  "sn4.6:0.2": "1. Lifespan ",
  "sn4.6:0.3": "A Cobra ",
  "sn4.6:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn4.6:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "sn4.6:1.3": "Now at that time the Buddha was meditating in the open during the dark of night, while a gentle rain drizzled down. ",
  "sn4.6:2.1": "Then Māra the Wicked, wanting to make the Buddha feel fear, terror, and goosebumps, manifested in the form of a big cobra king and approached him. ",
  "sn4.6:2.2": "Its body was like a big canoe carved from a single tree. ",
  "sn4.6:2.3": "",
  "sn4.6:2.4": "Its hood was like a large brewer’s sieve. ",
  "sn4.6:2.5": "",
  "sn4.6:2.6": "Its eyes were like big bronze cups from Kosala. ",
  "sn4.6:2.7": "",
  "sn4.6:2.8": "Its tongue flickered from its mouth like lightning flashes in a thunderstorm. ",
  "sn4.6:2.9": "",
  "sn4.6:2.10": "The sound of its breathing was like the puffing of a blacksmith’s bellows. ",
  "sn4.6:2.11": "",
  "sn4.6:3.1": "Then the Buddha, knowing that this was Māra the Wicked, replied to him in verse: ",
  "sn4.6:4.1": "“One who frequents empty buildings ",
  "sn4.6:4.2": "for lodging—that sage is self-restrained. ",
  "sn4.6:4.3": "It’s appropriate for that sort ",
  "sn4.6:4.4": "to live there after relinquishing. ",
  "sn4.6:5.1": "Though there are lots of creepy crawlies, ",
  "sn4.6:5.2": "and lots of flies and reptiles, ",
  "sn4.6:5.3": "they wouldn’t stir a h